markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Crafting Stories Project Overview 

#### In this project, students will be a data scientist tasked with answering questions and telling a data story. 

#### The will go through the Data Cycle: choose a dataset, ask RSAIR questions, clean and/or filter the data, create visualizations to help you analyze, answer, and possibly even develop more questions, and build a story around the data, thinking about the ethical concerns at every step.


<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 0; font-weight: bold;">In this project, students will:</h4>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt">
      <li>Ask a data question that is Relevant, Specific, Actionable, Investigative, and Respectful.
</li> <br>
    <li>Create clear data visualizations that provide insight into your data question.

</li><br>
        <li>Write a data story, with supporting evidence, to answer your data question.
        </li><br>
        <li>Describe the process you took through the data cycle.
        </li><br>
        <li>Examine any ethical concerns you encountered through the project. 
        </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <img src="https://images.code.org/4e1b6412c687590c048f087cef0675e6-image-1741789708762.png" 
         alt="Icon of clipboard and pen" 
         style="border-radius: 10px; width: 300px; height: auto;">
  </div>
</div>

## Project Requirements


<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">🧠 Data Question
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### Asks a data question that meets all five criteria: relevant, specific, actionable, investigative, and respectful.


</p></div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">🎨 Data Visualizations</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### Creates at least three clear and detailed visualizations using Google Sheets, each addressing different aspects of the data question. 


</p></div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">✅ Answer to Data Question</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### Provides a thorough answer to the data question, supported by multiple specific examples from the visualizations

</p></div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">📝 Final Response</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### A comprehensive final response includes all of the following: context of the data, shape of distribution, measures of center, answer to the data question, specific evidence from visualizations, and reflection on the answer. 


</p></div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">🔄 Data Cycle
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### Completes all data cycle steps: dataset selection, dataset decisions, data filtering, and trend analysis.

</p></div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">💜 Ethical Concerns
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### Thoroughly examines ethical concerns, discussing privacy, bias, and potential misuse with specific examples related to their dataset.

</p></div>
</details>

<br>

<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;">
    ➡️ Check out the full <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T3wQ5pdFj8ou59eEiK4UZXWla6t7Ejc-_mOA8RWeb_E/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.xe9cnc3216z0">Exemplar</a> to see how these concepts come to life in the classroom..
</p>
MARKDOWN
